# GCU400 specialization of _adaptive_avg_pool3d / _adaptive_avg_pool3d_out.
#
# Two launch shapes:
#   * lane  -- one lane per output element, pooling window walked as a masked
#     fixed-trip loop. Parallelism equals the output count, so it wins on large
#     outputs over narrow windows.
#   * tile  -- BO output elements x BR window offsets per program, reduced with
#     tl.sum(axis=1). Parallelism also covers the window, so it wins on small
#     outputs over wide windows.
# Both shapes have a single-pass form (grid == block count, no loop) and a
# grid-stride form used only when the flat block count would exceed the GCU400
# grid.x cap of 65535. The one-program-per-output kernel this replaces raised
# OutOfResources at 175616 outputs.
#
# Accumulation is float32 for every input dtype: GCU400 has no FP64 vector path
# (float64 tensors are stored as float32), so an FP64 accumulator would only
# mislead the compiler into an unsupported lowering.

